    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1513">

                <pb facs="0975" n="859" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg859"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.41/170.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Letcher to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">El Paso</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-03-04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 4, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Committee of three appointed by Carranza to examine into circumstances death of
                    Benton arrived here to-day and received later telegraphic instructions to the
                    effect that they should proceed to investigate case with a view to determining
                    whether a disinterment of the body of Benton is necessary or not. It was
                    reported here this afternoon that the committee would probably go to Chihuahua
                    by train to-morrow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Letcher</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
